== (4) the 2-adic contrast, measured ==
 aliquot: for even n <= 2000000, P(v_2(s(n)) = b | v_2(n) = a) (rows a = 1..6, columns b = 0..6, valuations >= 6 pooled):
   a = 1: [0.001, 0.895, 0.052, 0.026, 0.013, 0.007, 0.007]  mean log_2(s(n)/n) = -0.348 (n = 499999)
   a = 2: [0.001, 0.111, 0.747, 0.07, 0.035, 0.018, 0.017]  mean log_2(s(n)/n) = +0.129 (n = 250000)
   a = 3: [0.002, 0.118, 0.145, 0.566, 0.085, 0.042, 0.042]  mean log_2(s(n)/n) = +0.318 (n = 125000)
   a = 4: [0.003, 0.125, 0.15, 0.172, 0.382, 0.084, 0.084]  mean log_2(s(n)/n) = +0.404 (n = 62500)
   a = 5: [0.004, 0.134, 0.154, 0.176, 0.169, 0.235, 0.128]  mean log_2(s(n)/n) = +0.445 (n = 31250)
   a = 6: [0.01, 0.155, 0.165, 0.184, 0.168, 0.121, 0.198]  mean log_2(s(n)/n) = +0.472 (n = 31250)
 reading: the 2-adic valuation is sticky (the diagonal dominates for a >= 2) and the drift is negative only for a = 1: drivers persist for free
 Collatz: P(next valuation = b | current = a) along orbits of odd n < 2*10^5 (rows a = 1..6, columns b = 1..6; Terras: 2^(-b), independent of a):
