 reading: Collatz valuations are memoryless (each row is the geometric law), so a growth pattern must be paid for in advance by the residue; aliquot valuations are not
== (5) leaves and cycles ==
 untouchable numbers below 632 (exact scan: preimages m <= n^2 covered): [2, 5, 52, 88, 96, 120, 124, 146, 162, 188, 206, 210] ... count 52, density 0.082 (Erdos: positive density; Collatz's Syracuse leaves, the multiples of 3, have density exactly 1/3)
 even perfect numbers below 400000: [6, 28, 496, 8128] = triangular numbers T_(2^p - 1) with 2^p - 1 prime: True
 the same Mersenne indices 2^p - 1 are where the Catalan numbers are odd (seventh note); Euclid-Euler needs 2^p - 1 prime, Kummer needs nothing
